      "dom_id": "question-51559",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The $8$th and $9$th terms of an arithmetic sequence are $17$ and $21,$ respectively. Determine the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence.",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term is given by \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\n$$\n\nso we need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$ \n\nSince the terms ${a}_{8}=17$ and ${a}_{9}=21$ are consecutive, we can subtract them to find the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{9}-{a}_{8} \\\\  & =21-17 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use one of our known values, say, ${a}_{8}=17,$ to determine the first term of the sequence. Since ${a}_{8}$ is $7$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{8} & ={a}_{1}+7d \\\\ 17 & ={a}_{1}+7(4) \\\\ 17 & ={a}_{1}+28 \\\\ 17-28 & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term of this arithmetic sequence is:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-11+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =-11+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n-15\\end{aligned}\n$$",
